<title>USA: TABLE - Silver Diner Inc Q2 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Silver Diner Inc Q2 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>ROCKVILLE, Md. 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve Weeks Ended   Twenty-Eight Weeks Ended</p>
<p>			Jul 13,     Jul 14,	Jul 13,    Jul 14,</p>
<p>			  1997	  1996	   1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net sales    $ 6,011,695 $ 3,974,420 $ 12,143,899 $8,868,848</p>
<p>	NET LOSS  (409,559)   (248,137)  (1,157,621)  (946,228)</p>
<p>Net loss per</p>
<p>  common share     (0.04)	(0.02)	 (0.10)     (0.12)</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>		   11,634,642  10,075,287   11,600,752  7,853,126</p>
<p>NOTE:  Company said the increase in sales in second-quarter 1997 was due to  sales generated by four new restaurants opened since December 1996 in northern Virginia.</p>
<p>Also said widening of the net loss for second-quarter 1997 was due to an increase in the weighted average number of shares outstanding from about 7.9 million shares to 11.6 million as a result of its merger with Food Trends Acquisition Corp in March 1996 and a private equity placement in July 1996.</p>
</text>
